# REBASH Academy Style Guide

Voice:

Professional

Friendly

Educational

Practical

Avoid:

Buzzwords

Marketing

Filler

Corporate jargon

Always explain acronyms on first use.

Examples:

Infrastructure as Code (IaC)

Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)

Site Reliability Engineering (SRE)

Container Storage Interface (CSI)

Be consistent throughout the documentation.

Prefer active voice.

Use British English spelling consistently unless quoting commands or official product names.

Keep terminology consistent across all tutorials.

---

## Brand logos and icons

Use real brand logos and Material Design Icons — never invent placeholder glyphs.

- Nav / `.pages`: `icon: material/<brand>` (e.g. `material/docker`, `material/aws`, `material/gitlab`, `material/kubernetes`, `material/terraform`, `material/linux`, `material/git`).
- Landing cards (`overrides/home.html`, `overrides/learning-paths.html`): import `mdi` from `partials/rebash-icons.html` and call `{{ mdi("docker") }}` (same icon names as Material).
- Site chrome: keep the REBASH `logo.svg` / favicon assets; do not replace them with generated stand-ins.
- Social links: Font Awesome brand icons in `mkdocs.yml` (`fontawesome/brands/...`).
